han C's unwillingness to develop, which could affect long-term safety. So she might shift to C. But she also might want more info on D.\n\nGiven that we have not yet covered D, we might want to bring D into discussion before final recommendation. However we need to give a provisional vote now. We could say we remain with B but we need to discuss D and A before final. That aligns with earlier plan.\n\nThus Sarah's public message: \"I understand James's emphasis on B's reliability and technical competence, but I remain uneasy about his uncooperative, pretentious behavior, which directly impacts crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014critical for long-haul flights. Candidate C, while having communication difficulties, demonstrates perfect reliability, calmness in crisis, quick correct decisions, and a positive crew atmosphere, which may outweigh B's interpersonal issues. Moreover, we still lack data on D's stress resilience and crew cooperation. Therefore, I am shifting my provisional recommendation to Candidate C, pending further discussion of D and A.\" That would be a shift.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at weather, computer skills, can be grumpy, uncooperative, pretentious, wrong tone. C 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, keeps calm in crisis, makes correct decisions quickly, excellent attention, difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nWe must give metadata JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nLet's produce that."}
